// BNC C Output Control Example
// This script configures BNC C as an output and controls its state
// BNC A and B are reserved for triggers
//
// Simple syntax:
//   bnc 0          - Set BNC C output LOW
//   bnc 1          - Set BNC C output HIGH
//   bnc 0 delay:X  - Set LOW with X ms delay after
//
// The bnc command uses CFG_BNC_C register (0x082) internally:
//   - bnc 0: DIR=1, INV=0 (0x200) -> output LOW
//   - bnc 1: DIR=1, INV=1 (0x300) -> output HIGH

// Example: Toggle BNC C with timing
bnc 0                  // Set BNC C LOW
t += 1                 // Wait 1 ms in timeline
bnc 1                  // Set BNC C HIGH
t += 1                 // Wait 1 ms
bnc 0                  // Set BNC C LOW
t += 0.2               // Wait 200 us
bnc 1                  // Set BNC C HIGH
t += 0.2
bnc 0                  // Set BNC C LOW
